safix::no_store_database

  × flake.safix.keepassxc declares 3 mapping(s) and no database, so there
  │ is nothing for them to converge against.
  │ 
  │ There is no default and there cannot be one: which database holds a
  │ person's credentials is a fact about their machine. Name it as a string
  │ rather than a nix path — a path is copied into the store when it is
  │ interpolated, and the store is world-readable:
  │ 
  │     flake.safix.keepassxc.database = "/home/<you>/.keys/master.kdbx";
